      "writtenOn": "2025-02-12T23:03:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "BluetoothServerSocket#accept() is not interruptible. It is blocking on a read() on a unix socket without SO_RCVTIMEO. The only way to interrupt is is by calling shutdown(SHUT_RD), which is what BluetoothServerSocket#close() does before it actually closes the underlying fd.\n\nre race: (I should really leave a comment along these lines): I agree that there is a race, though because all code paths always refer to the handler thread and (more importantly) always check that the offer still exists, this shouldn\u0027t be a problem. In fact, the check for !mIsRunning is mostly for preventing the log statement below. Calling postDestroyAndUnregisterReservedOffer() on the teardown path is totally fine, as it will just return early because the offer was removed from the set.",
      "parentUuid": "4bf18579_848f3793",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 318,
        "startChar": 29,
        "endLine": 318,
        "endChar": 39
      },
